{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734629-did-these-guys-even-bother-reading-werewolf-the-apocalypse","id":734629,"title":"Did these guys even bother reading Werewolf: The Apocalypse?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-28T07:15:58-07:00","id":734629,"title":"Did these guys even bother reading Werewolf: The Apocalypse?","content":"<a href=\"http://io9.com/all-14-werewolf-tribes-of-werewolf-the-apocalypse-ran-1738988364\" target=\"_blank\">Sigh. </a>It's time like this when I really wonder why I even occasionally look at io9. If the stuff I know less about is covered with this much expertise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:29:13-07:00","id":734659,"title":"","content":"Hahaha! Oh my that's wonderful. In an insight to how others may view it.<br /> <br /> my favourite though has to be some of the informed comments left on the comment section. This particular one is my favourite.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think the Black Spiral Dancers were called the Roanoke before their fall. I know they were the third Native tribe.&quot;<br /> <br /> This can mean only thing folks, we must double our efforts to open this wonderful game to others and portray as much as possible in truly wonderful and epic experiences for all to enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:33:04-07:00","id":734670,"title":"","content":"I didn't even read it yet, but Cracked has taught me that general if some article begins with &quot;list of X things that are Y&quot; or soemthing like that then it's clickbait and anything in there cna be safely discarded<br /> Which is not to say they are not fun to read, just more concerned with flair than being informative","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:46:01-07:00","id":734707,"title":"","content":"Sometimes, it's a matter of only reading older books, too. Like the thing about the Black Furies murdering most of their male children, which was mentioned perhaps once, and is from the same book that the cropped art in the article is (first edition player's guide). But then you get to the &quot;weren't they called Roanoke?&quot; thing, and, urgh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:51:20-07:00","id":734743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734629-did-these-guys-even-bother-reading-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=734707#post734707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes, it's a matter of only reading older books, too. Like the thing about the Black Furies murdering most of their male children, which was mentioned perhaps once, and is from the same book that the cropped art in the article is (first edition player's guide). But then you get to the &quot;weren't they called Roanoke?&quot; thing, and, urgh.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty amazing how that and the Fenrir racism, despite being only one thing in the books, tend to stick with people like glue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T07:58:37-07:00","id":734764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734629-did-these-guys-even-bother-reading-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=734743#post734743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's pretty amazing how that and the Fenrir racism, despite being only one thing in the books, tend to stick with people like glue.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the solvent that is the Revised Tribebook doesn't seem to be powerful enough to remove it. In spite of the fact that it's been out for roughly thirteen years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T08:06:19-07:00","id":734773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734629-did-these-guys-even-bother-reading-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=734764#post734764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the solvent that is the Revised Tribebook doesn't seem to be powerful enough to remove it. In spite of the fact that it's been out for roughly thirteen years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it could simply be the ignorance of them. And given I've seen far too many people cling to houserules as canon in online games, what people first played the game as tends to be seen as canon no matter what changes are made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T14:01:57-07:00","id":735748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734629-did-these-guys-even-bother-reading-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=734670#post734670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is not to say they are not fun to read, just more concerned with flair than being informative</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately the flaw in the article is that is isn't either, because it's so ridiculously ignorant of the game. If it was a flair oriented list that was written more as a satire of the Tribes, it would be amusing; but that require actually knowing the game well enough to actually be able to put in the nods and winks to show you're doing that.<br /> <br /> I mean, this is a list that says the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords are useless because WtA has no political arenas, as all werewolves just hang out with their packs... even though Septs and the politics of them, have always been a prominent part of the setting. Even just having the 1e Core book would tell you that. Lots of the lore/mechanical things that the listicle gets wrong could at least be chalked up to edition differences and memories being imperfect, and still be an amusing.<br /> <br /> It's not fun to read, because if you know enough about WtA to understand (or care) you'd know how stupid the writing is, and if you don't know enough, there isn't really context to understand (and if you looked up any of it on the Internet, you'd quickly get confused as hell as to what the hell this listicle is on about).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T23:32:48-07:00","id":737109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734629-did-these-guys-even-bother-reading-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=735748#post735748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not fun to read, because if you know enough about WtA to understand (or care) you'd know how stupid the writing is, and if you don't know enough, there isn't really context to understand (and if you looked up any of it on the Internet, you'd quickly get confused as hell as to what the hell this listicle is on about).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't know, I showed it to my group and we all had a hearty guffaw.<br /> <br /> The Fenrir player was not surprised to see his tribe at the top of the list- but all pride left him when he read the reasoning behind the Get's lofty ranking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T12:20:14-07:00","id":739270,"title":"","content":"The most hilarious moment of Lex Luthor yelling &quot;WROOOONG!&quot; is probably the Red Talon entry. &quot;No, really, they can put this aside easily and be a normal fixture of a general campaign.&quot; Ha. Ha. Huh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:50:50-07:00","id":739537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734629-did-these-guys-even-bother-reading-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=739270#post739270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most hilarious moment of Lex Luthor yelling &quot;WROOOONG!&quot; is probably the Red Talon entry. &quot;No, really, they can put this aside easily and be a normal fixture of a general campaign.&quot; Ha. Ha. Huh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would hazard a guess that this is due to him and his group being a pack of rage-fueled murderhobos. If they were already planning on fighting and killing everyone all the time anyway, the Red Talon's particular hatred of humans is little more than an amusing pecadillo.<br /> <br /> I was also confused/enraged that the Wendigo are supposed to be awesome 'ninjas' according to Mr. Bricken, while the Uktena are scarcely more than Wyrmy racist stereotypes. The Uktena are noted for having a lot of dispossessed cultures united within their tribe, while the Wendigo are xenophobes who are almost all one race- in what universe are the Uktena stereotypical 'red skins' but the Wendigo are both literally and figuratively super cool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-29-2015, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:10:49-07:00","id":739588,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Children of Gaia are peace loving-pacifists...&quot; Ugh, NO. The CoGs prefer to deal diplomatically with people who can be persuaded to be allies against the Wyrm but they are most certainly NOT pacifists. They have Rage just like any other Garou, they just keep better control of it (for the most part) and aren't afraid to claw and bite minions of the Wyrm if there's no other alternative. There are a few literal pacifists among the Coggies, but they're a small minority of the tribe.<br /> <br /> The CoGs may be among the most misunderstood tribes (if not the most misunderstood), but anyone with half a brain and has read Werewolf knows or should know that the CoGs are still <i>werewolves</i>. They're willing to fight, but they'd just prefer to fight smarter rather than harder, because that's more effective in the long run than a war of attrition when you're outnumbered 10 to 1 by the Wyrm's troops.<br /> <br /> Yeah, this isn't the most egregious part of the essay by any means, but after reading this, I can't help but think that the author REALLY doesn't know what he's talking about. This doesn't read like satire at all to me either because there aren't any in-the-know jokes that I can see. None of it strikes me as funny in any case. I can see why some Werewolf players would find it funny as something to laugh at the ignorance of someone who doesn't know what he's talking about. But it doesn't seem funny to me, just annoying.<br /> <br /> But then, people lacking self-awareness are a pet peeve of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 10-29-2015, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:37:16-07:00","id":739661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734629-did-these-guys-even-bother-reading-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=739537#post739537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would hazard a guess that this is due to him and his group being a pack of rage-fueled murderhobos. If they were already planning on fighting and killing everyone all the time anyway, the Red Talon's particular hatred of humans is little more than an amusing pecadillo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, I've heard a lot of people who like werewolves bemoan that WtA hasn't really got 'true' werewolves as monsters who kill people. While this is particularly incorrect, it is entirely possible this guy's group played their WtA games more akin to traditional werewolf rampages than anything else. Hence why ignorance of sept politics and focus on killing vampires.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:44:11-07:00","id":739678,"title":"","content":"After reading through it, this reminds me of how a lot of people viewed WtA when it first came out. I remember a lot of people describing it to others as Fury Boy Scouts, Fury Eco Terrorists or Captain Planet with teeth. In fact for a long time, I remember a number of WtA games being ran that way at our store. Very few of the games had the characters packs even interacting with any other Garou at all. They just went around attacking and destroying corporations that were destroying the environment while battling the Wyrm minion of the week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T03:43:19-07:00","id":741252,"title":"","content":"This article in no way reminds me of all the things I like about Werewolf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Similar for their list of Vampire clans, for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T03:58:54-07:00","id":741283,"title":"","content":"And funnily enough, we're all reading it. So, from the perspective of the authors... mission accomplished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T04:20:03-07:00","id":741294,"title":"","content":"Curse their clickbait-laden house!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T05:23:24-07:00","id":744266,"title":"","content":"Clickbait has to be GW ragabash name somewhere. Hmm but weren't the GWs originally called the The Get of Gaea before they fell to the Weaver in 1987? Really good fighters though.<br /> <br /> ((Yes I did that all wrong intentionally and wonder if it'll turn up on the next WtA clickbait listings <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}